---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import ToolVote from '../../../components/ToolVote.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="FlowLens"
  description="A Garmin watch app that answers four questions people already ask themselves and mostly answer by guessing — from your own history, never a population norm. Partly built."
>
  <main class="reading" id="main">
    <section class="block insight-page">
      <p class="kicker"><a href="/tools/">Tools</a></p>
      <h1>FlowLens</h1>

      <p class="lede">
        Four questions people already ask themselves, and mostly answer by guessing. This is a watch app that
        answers them from your own history instead.
      </p>

      <ul class="ask-list">
        <li>How long into the weekend before I am back to myself after a hard week at the office?</li>
        <li>When on an ordinary day is my stress actually down — and is it ever down at work?</li>
        <li>My family says I come home stressed. Are they right, and how often?</li>
        <li>Which hours are genuinely mine — and what did that meeting cost to get through?</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What it does</h2>

      <p>
        It watches the week hour by hour rather than as a daily average, because a day that started well and
        fell apart after lunch should not look like a day that was mediocre throughout.
      </p>

      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li>
          <strong>It says when it does not know yet.</strong> On the day it is installed it counts the days
          remaining and calls itself calibrating rather than starting. The confidence model decides what counts
          as a finding; it does not get to decide what you are allowed to look at.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Conditions, not verdicts.</strong> "You work best on Tuesday" does not transfer to a
          Thursday. Morning, at home, a recovered start and ninety clear minutes does.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The slide a weekly view cannot see.</strong> Nobody goes downhill by having one bad Tuesday.
          They have two months where each Tuesday is slightly worse than the last, and no single day of it
          looks alarming enough to mention.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Almost everything is a comparison against your own history — never a population norm, never a clinical
        reading. The one exception exists because self-reference fails in a specific way: someone whose normal
        is bad gets told they are fine, reliably, forever.
      </p>

      <h2>The walkthrough</h2>

      <p>
        Twenty-one frames on a fēnix 9 Pro, from the day it is installed to the conditions it eventually
        learns. What is built is badged as running; the rest is drawn to argue the shape.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="demo-wide">
      <iframe
        id="flowlens-demo"
        src="/tools/flowlens-demo.html"
        title="FlowLens walkthrough"
        loading="lazy"
        scrolling="no"
      ></iframe>
      <p class="demo-fallback">
        <a href="/tools/flowlens-demo.html">Open the walkthrough on its own</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="block insight-page">
      <ToolVote tool="flowlens" />
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .insight-page h2 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin: 2.6rem 0 0.7rem;
  }
  .ask-list {
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding: 0 0 0 1.2rem;
    list-style: none;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--mist);
  }
  .ask-list li {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }
  .feature-list {
    margin: 1.4rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }
  .feature-list li {
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }
  .feature-list strong {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  /* The walkthrough is wider than the reading measure, so it steps out of the
     column to the shell width the rest of the site uses. */
  .demo-wide {
    width: min(65rem, calc(100vw - 3rem));
    margin: 2rem 0 3.4rem 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
  }
  /* On a phone the reading gutter is worth more to the walkthrough than to the
     margin: the watch and its readout have a floor they cannot shrink past. */
  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .demo-wide {
      width: 100vw;
    }
  }
  .demo-wide iframe {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 1400px;
    border: 0;
  }
  .demo-fallback {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
    font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Same-origin, so the height can be measured directly rather than posted
  // across, and the site's theme toggle can be handed through to the frame.
  const frame = document.getElementById('flowlens-demo') as HTMLIFrameElement | null;

  if (frame) {
    const syncTheme = () => {
      const doc = frame.contentDocument;
      if (!doc) return;
      const theme = document.documentElement.dataset.theme;
      if (theme) doc.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;
      else delete doc.documentElement.dataset.theme;
    };

    const syncHeight = () => {
      const doc = frame.contentDocument;
      if (!doc?.body) return;
      frame.style.height = `${doc.body.scrollHeight + 8}px`;
    };

    const wire = () => {
      syncTheme();
      syncHeight();
      const doc = frame.contentDocument;
      if (doc?.body && 'ResizeObserver' in window) {
        new ResizeObserver(syncHeight).observe(doc.body);
      }
      // The walkthrough advances on its own, and each frame is a different height.
      setInterval(syncHeight, 1000);
    };

    frame.addEventListener('load', wire);
    // A lazy frame can finish before this script runs, in which case the load
    // event has already been and gone.
    if (frame.contentDocument?.readyState === 'complete') wire();

    new MutationObserver(syncTheme).observe(document.documentElement, {
      attributes: true,
      attributeFilter: ['data-theme'],
    });
  }
</script>
